WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:03.570
-I've heard tell that the set
in the Catskills was haunted.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.537 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Is there truth to this?

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we'd heard
there was a ghost.

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.509 line:92%
It was a very, very old resort.

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:10.310 line:92%
We heard there was a ghost.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.646
Thankfully, we didn't shoot
in the building where the ghost

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:16.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
haunted or however that works.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:16.850 line:92%
But we heard some weird --

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.252
-And it's nice, by the way, that
the ghost stays to one building.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
-And let's you work around.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:21.554 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-That's exactly right.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.223 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're very grateful
to the ghost.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:26.826
We just had some weird stuff
happen while we were there.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you buy into it?
-Well...

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.597 line:92%
Okay, so here's the thing.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:34.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
I did not buy in to
the whole ghost thing until --

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:38.171 size:88% position:44%
A couple of years ago,
we shot my final episode

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:40.407 line:92%
of "House of Cards" in Santa Fe.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, we shot it in Las Vegas,
New Mexico,

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:45.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was about
an hour outside of Santa Fe.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:46.312 line:92%
-It's very disappointing.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
It could not be more different
than Las Vegas, Nevada.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:50.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Couldn't be --

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.684 line:92%
The first time I saw the sign,

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really thought
we were going to Las Vegas.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was very confused
by Las Vegas.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My wife's family
is from near Albuquerque,

00:00:57.457 --> 00:00:58.324 line:92%
and the first time I visited,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.493 size:88% position:44%
you see a sign that says
"Las Vegas, 100 miles."

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, "Here we go."
-It's so close.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's not the same, no.
-It's not, no.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:07.567 size:88% position:44%
-Las Vegas, New Mexico,
is kind of a ghost town.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:10.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They say -- They call it
"The city that always sleeps."

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.240 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's really good.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.010
But we stayed
in this hotel called The Plaza.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.245 size:81% position:41%
A little bit different
from the Plaza here.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:24.150
And -- And, you know, basically,
I walked into my room there

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:27.120
and was overcome
with this really weird feeling,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.021 size:81% position:41% line:92%
which is so unlike me.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just walked in,
and it felt so strange.

00:01:30.290 --> 00:01:31.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've never
done this in my life,

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I went downstairs,
and I sort of said

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.161 line:92%
to the front desk girl --

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was really
embarrassed about it.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Would you --
I'm sorry.

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:40.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you have
another room available?

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:41.401 line:92%
Do you mind if I swap rooms?"

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.570 size:84% position:42%
And she looked at me
in what I now feel like

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.707 size:88% position:44%
was a really knowing way
and kind of went, "Yes.

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:50.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll give you a room
in the new wing."

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh!
-Gave me another room,

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I walked into the room
in the new wing

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.416 line:92%
and was twice as creeped out.

00:01:56.416 --> 00:01:58.118 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Like, really was like --

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm having
all these weird feelings.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went back down,
I was like, "I'm so, so sorry,

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm actually
gonna take the first room.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you mind?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
Spent the night
in the first room,

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.393 line:92%
was like, "I'm being a freak."

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:10.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the next morning, woke up,
and flying around set

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.600
were these rumors
that one of our transpo guys --

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
big, masculine,
kind of scary dude --

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:19.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
had woken up
in the middle of the night

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.840 line:92%
because he heard this big crash.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he kind of went,
"Who's there?"

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:24.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
And someone said,
"Oh, don't mind me.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm just
looking for my jewelry."

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.581
And he marches downstairs
and goes, "What the heck?

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.151
You can't send someone into my
room in the middle of the night.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is completely
inappropriate."

00:02:32.285 --> 00:02:34.687
And the woman at the desk went,
"Oh, don't mind her.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:38.091
That's just Cassandra.
She's looking for her jewelry."

00:02:38.091 --> 00:02:38.625 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:42.629
And we're all freaking out
and running around the set,

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:45.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
going, "We can't stay here.
We have to leave."

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I believe in ghosts
literally because

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of our New Mexican
crew members went,

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:53.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, don't worry about it.
Completely harmless.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:54.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you want them
to leave you alone,

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:57.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
just leave an offering
and thank them

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.945 line:92%
for sharing the space with you

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:01.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
and ask them to just
leave you alone tonight."

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:02.916 line:92%
So I went back to the hotel.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:03.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm on the phone
with a friend of mine,

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:07.587
who I'm expecting to go,
"You know, you're being a freak.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stop."
And instead my friend goes,

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Run, get out.
Get another hotel."

00:03:11.257 --> 00:03:12.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"Leave immediately."

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:14.527
So I'm on the phone with my
friend, who's going, "Run,"

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm --
I've got these banana chips,

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.831 size:84% position:42%
and I'm laying them out
on the table, going --

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Banana chips?!
-Banana chips!

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.467 line:92%
It was all I had with me.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:24.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
I hope they like organic food.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:25.238 line:92%
"Thank you so much for sharing."

00:03:25.238 --> 00:03:27.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They're like,
"I died 100 years ago.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.241 line:92%
You can't give me potato chips?"

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:29.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's ri--
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:31.811
I'm like, "Thank you so much
for sharing the space with me.

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:33.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please leave me alone."
[ Laughing ]

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And how did it go?
Did you feel that --

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:36.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you get
a better night's sleep?

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
-Okay. Well...

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's the truth, so I'm --
-There you go.

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm a convert.
I believe in ghosts.

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:43.957
But, thankfully, the Catskills
ghost left us to our business.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:46.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. And now I'm assuming
you always travel

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:47.927
with banana chips just in case.
-Always.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:51.297 size:84% position:42%
Always, always, always.
-This is -- a lot of --

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.632 line:92%
I would imagine a lot of people,

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:53.866 size:84% position:42%
even though you've had
an accomplished career,

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
this is the favorite role
you've played.

00:03:55.702 --> 00:03:57.937 line:92%
Your parents love "Maisel."

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They love "Maisel."
I am alive.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:03.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have my clothes on
most of the time.

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:04.077 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.979 line:92%
I'm not crying and depressed.

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:07.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
They are thrilled.
-That's wonderful.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:10.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very sweetly,
my dad calls me all the time

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:13.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
and says that he's re-watched
certain episodes,

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and he quotes them.

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:16.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is absolutely
my parents' favorite --

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really sweet!
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:04:18.258 --> 00:04:19.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is great.
And it's real --

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, again, as an actor,
you never know

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:23.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you're gonna do anything...
-Yeah.

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.097 line:92%
-...that your parents like.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.299
They might be proud of you
and also watch other shows,

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it's really wonderful
that both --

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:28.401 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:32.572
-I mean, my dad may or may not
have ever seen "House of Cards."

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:33.172 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's thrilled.

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it wasn't real
until this show.

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, by the way,
if I were your dad,

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:38.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would have trouble
watching "House of Cards."

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.713
It was not a great road for you.
-No.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:44.183
I mean, you know, I got zip-tied
and thrown in the back of a van.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:45.285 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It didn't end well.

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.020 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Spoiler alert!
-Spoiler alert!

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:48.621 line:92%
Do you still have to say that?

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:51.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's been six years!
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:53.660 line:92%
Maybe you were the ghost.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:54.560 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:57.163 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:57.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-Wow.

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:01.834 size:78% position:39%
This got really deep.
-This is really...

